cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata.
type: software
title: shadowbank-screen
abstract: >-
  Screens wire activity against the findings in FinCEN's Financial Trend Analysis "Iranian Shadow
  Banking: Update on Trends in Bank Secrecy Act Data" (November 23, 2026): bank-location routes to
  the UAE, registration and banking splits, free-zone and Marshall Islands or BVI registration at
  shared addresses, and, for many companies, little to no web presence, opaque ownership,
  co-location or recent incorporation; multimillion wires with missing or incomplete
  source-of-funds information, or a mismatch with the line of business, bursts, absent operating
  expenses and shared counterparties. Clusters flagged parties, estimates activity not yet
  attributed with chain-ladder development (FinCEN cited Friedland's chapter; Mack standard errors
  are this tool's choice), and back-tests each check against recorded outcomes. Engineering
  checklist, not legal advice. Tested on synthetic data only.
authors:
